cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "STUR-ROLL: cosmic birefringence from integers"
abstract: >-
  A Z2-odd U(1) holonomy on an S1/Z2 orbifold couples to photons through a
  5D Chern-Simons term at integer level k. A smooth birth fixes the holonomy
  at zero; a parity-fixed brane twist turns that point into a hilltop; the
  late roll by pi rotates CMB polarization by beta = k alpha / 2 = 0.2091 deg
  for k = 1, with no fitted parameter. Testable by LiteBIRD through the
  amplitude and the tomographic difference.
authors:
